Drain the log pipe at exit under the threaded logger's lock

With --log-master, the uWSGI 2.0.31 master reads its workers' log lines
from a pipe into the global buffer `uwsgi.log_master_buf` and writes
them out. With --threaded-logger, a master thread does that read and
write in `uwsgi_master_log` (core/logging.c), holding
`uwsgi.threaded_logger_lock`. At exit, the atexit handler
`uwsgi_flush_logs` (core/uwsgi.c) drains what is left in the pipe from
the main thread. It allocates a new `uwsgi.log_master_buf` every time
and reads without the lock. When the thread has read a line but not yet
written it, the swap makes it write uninitialized heap memory of that
line's length instead, and the line is lost; both threads also read the
pipe at once.

The CobaltCore API containers run uWSGI with --threaded-logger
(`UWSGIGracefulShutdownArgs` in internal/common/deployment/uwsgi.go).
The master logs `gateway "uWSGI http 1" has been buried` and
`goodbye to uWSGI.` right before it exits, so the race hits the last
lines of every container log. Measured in 40 start/SIGTERM cycles of the
keystone 2026.1 image with those flags: unpatched, 25 logs carried a
record of NUL bytes and heap pointers, 24 of them in place of the buried
line, 31 logged `goodbye to uWSGI.` twice and 2 not at all; patched, 40
of 40 logs carried both lines once and no such record. The image check
below failed 15 of 20 runs unpatched and passed 30 of 30 patched.

The patch allocates the buffer only when none exists, and drains the
pipe under the lock the thread holds, so a line is read and written by
one thread from one buffer. Only the master takes the lock: the other
processes that run this handler fork from the master and may inherit
the mutex locked, and none of them runs the thread.

`assert_uwsgi_graceful_shutdown` in tests/lib/uwsgi.sh, which the verify
scripts of the eight uWSGI API images call, fails when the log carries
`goodbye to uWSGI.` other than exactly once, or a byte outside
printable ASCII, tab and newline.

nix/lib/python-env.nix applies the patch to the uwsgi source of every
lock with `patch --fuzz=0`. A uWSGI release that moves these lines, or
already carries the fix, fails the build there.

Applies to uWSGI 2.0.31 (nix/base-requirements.txt).

Upstream status: not reported; tracked in #1635.

diff --git a/core/uwsgi.c b/core/uwsgi.c
index 5316efe..d0a1dd4 100644
--- a/core/uwsgi.c
+++ b/core/uwsgi.c
@@ -1925,10 +1925,17 @@ void uwsgi_flush_logs() {
 
 check:
 	// this buffer could not be initialized !!!
-	if (uwsgi.log_master) {
+	if (uwsgi.log_master && !uwsgi.log_master_buf) {
 		uwsgi.log_master_buf = uwsgi_malloc(uwsgi.log_master_bufsize);
 	}
 
+	// the master's threaded logger reads the same pipe into the same buffer
+	int locked = 0;
+	if (uwsgi.threaded_logger && uwsgi.workers && uwsgi.workers[0].pid == getpid()) {
+		pthread_mutex_lock(&uwsgi.threaded_logger_lock);
+		locked = 1;
+	}
+
 	// check for data in logpipe
 	pfd.events = POLLIN;
 	pfd.fd = uwsgi.shared->worker_log_pipe[0];
@@ -1940,6 +1947,9 @@ check:
 			break;
 		}
 	}
+
+	if (locked)
+		pthread_mutex_unlock(&uwsgi.threaded_logger_lock);
 }
 
